<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Tübingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1514">1514</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tübingen Treaty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tubingen">Tübingen</a> was an agreement of 8 July 1514 between Duke Ulrich of Württemberg and the estates of his duchy, made during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poor-conrad">Poor Conrad</a> revolt. The estates took over the duke's debts in return for the right to approve taxes and wars and guarantees of personal liberties. It became the foundation of Württemberg's constitution and limited ducal power until the early nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tubingen.jpg" alt="Treaty of Tübingen" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:900-123_T%C3%BCbinger_Vertrag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
